GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC13): the polygons of the picture on screen, for the cast shadows;
the game's own shadows left out while GoldLink casts its own.

- GPU3D_Soft: at each render the frame's polygons are kept (KeepGeometry): each vertex's clip
  coordinates, texture coordinates and screen position; each polygon's attributes, texture
  parameters and kind (attached, translucent, the DS's shadow volumes). Where an opaque polygon's
  texture format can have transparent texels, its texture's transparency is decoded once (kept
  until texture memory changes), so a sprite casts its silhouette. The next render makes them the
  shown picture's (GetShownGeometry), as the depth (0004).
- The game's own shadows (the blobs under people, a house's, a sign's or the windmill's painted
  shadow) are translucent polygons, dark grey and see-through over the texels they show
  (GameShadow): marked (ShadowGame), and with HideGameShadows left out of the render.

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

